  "scope": "A disposable Kubernetes v1.36.1 cluster runs two copies of a case-owned HTTP promotion gate against the same inert model identity: one enforcement-disabled baseline and one enforcing gate. The enabled gate authenticates a short-lived reporter ServiceAccount token with authentication.k8s.io/v1 TokenReview, accepts evidence only from that exact principal and audience, persists the submitted fixed evidence in a namespace-scoped ConfigMap, reads it back, and requires pass results for security, bias, performance and robustness plus matching builder/model/predicate digests. It records signature verification as unverified. This proves the fixture API/RBAC/TokenReview and deterministic policy path for fixed synthetic records only; it does not prove evaluator efficacy, genuine model quality, cryptographic signature trust, report-writer audit attribution, or production promotion workflow coverage.",
